 ],
 "captions": [
  {
   "from": 17,
   "to": 34,
   "text": "In the year 793, England's chroniclers"
  },
  {
   "from": 36,
   "to": 82,
   "text": "recorded something terrifying."
  },
  {
   "from": 84,
   "to": 159,
   "text": "\"Immense sheets of light rushing through the air,"
  },
  {
   "from": 161,
   "to": 202,
   "text": "and whirlwinds, and fiery dragons"
  },
  {
   "from": 204,
   "to": 255,
   "text": "flying across the firmament.\""
  },
  {
   "from": 257,
   "to": 321,
   "text": "Soon after, the Vikings came."
  },
  {
   "from": 322,
   "to": 388,
   "text": "They struck the holy island of Lindisfarne,"
  },
  {
   "from": 389,
   "to": 474,
   "text": "and the chronicle remembered those dragons as a warning."
  },
  {
   "from": 476,
   "to": 587,
   "text": "So what did medieval people actually believe a dragon was?"
  },
  {
   "from": 589,
   "to": 668,
   "text": "The answer is stranger than any movie."
  },
  {
   "from": 895,
   "to": 982,
   "text": "The word comes from the Latin \"draco\", a giant serpent."
  },
  {
   "from": 984,
   "to": 1074,
   "text": "Around the year 600, Isidore of Seville wrote the encyclopedia"
  },
  {
   "from": 1075,
   "to": 1170,
   "text": "that medieval Europe trusted most after the Bible."
  },
  {
   "from": 1171,
   "to": 1249,
   "text": "His dragon was the largest creature on Earth."
  },
  {
   "from": 1251,
   "to": 1312,
   "text": "It had a crest and a small mouth,"
  },
  {
   "from": 1313,
   "to": 1381,
   "text": "and its power was not in its teeth."
  },
  {
   "from": 1383,
   "to": 1414,
   "text": "It was in its tail."
  },
  {
   "from": 1415,
   "to": 1504,
   "text": "The bestiaries, the illustrated animal books of the twelfth"
  },
  {
   "from": 1505,
   "to": 1549,
   "text": "and thirteenth centuries, added the details."
  },
  {
   "from": 1551,
   "to": 1641,
   "text": "A dragon waited on the paths elephants used, knotted its"
  },
  {
   "from": 1643,
   "to": 1756,
   "text": "tail around their legs, and squeezed until they suffocated."
  },
  {
   "from": 1758,
   "to": 1843,
   "text": "It feared one animal above all: the panther,"
  },
  {
   "from": 1844,
   "to": 1917,
   "text": "whose sweet breath drew every creature to it,"
  },
  {
   "from": 1919,
   "to": 1994,
   "text": "except the dragon, which fled into hiding."
  },
  {
   "from": 1996,
   "to": 2080,
   "text": "And in these books, the dragon did not breathe fire."
  },
  {
   "from": 2082,
   "to": 2128,
   "text": "It didn't need to."
  },
  {
   "from": 2220,
   "to": 2271,
   "text": "The fire came from the poets."
  },
  {
   "from": 2273,
   "to": 2370,
   "text": "In Beowulf, a thief steals a jewelled cup from a dragon"
  },
  {
   "from": 2371,
   "to": 2480,
   "text": "sleeping on its treasure inside an ancient burial mound."
  },
  {
   "from": 2482,
   "to": 2558,
   "text": "The dragon wakes, and it burns the land,"
  },
  {
   "from": 2559,
   "to": 2608,
   "text": "the king's own hall included."
  },
  {
   "from": 2609,
   "to": 2675,
   "text": "The old king goes out to face it."
  },
  {
   "from": 2677,
   "to": 2714,
   "text": "His sword shatters."
  },
  {
   "from": 2715,
   "to": 2745,
   "text": "His men run."
  },
  {
   "from": 2746,
   "to": 2812,
   "text": "Only young Wiglaf stays beside him."
  },
  {
   "from": 2813,
   "to": 2937,
   "text": "Together they kill the dragon, but Beowulf dies of his wounds."
  },
  {
   "from": 2938,
   "to": 3035,
   "text": "It's often called medieval Europe's first fire-breathing dragon,"
  },
  {
   "from": 3037,
   "to": 3136,
   "text": "and the poem survives in exactly one manuscript."
  },
  {
   "from": 3137,
   "to": 3232,
   "text": "In 1731 that manuscript was caught in a library fire."
  },
  {
   "from": 3233,
   "to": 3308,
   "text": "You can still see where its edges burned."
  },
  {
   "from": 3309,
   "to": 3372,
   "text": "Further north, the Norse told of F\u00e1fnir,"
  },
  {
   "from": 3374,
   "to": 3461,
   "text": "so greedy for cursed gold that he killed his own father"
  },
  {
   "from": 3463,
   "to": 3516,
   "text": "and became a serpent coiled on it."
  },
  {
   "from": 3518,
   "to": 3567,
   "text": "The hero Sigurd hid in a pit"
  },
  {
   "from": 3568,
   "to": 3639,
   "text": "and stabbed upward as the dragon passed."
  },
  {
   "from": 3640,
   "to": 3728,
   "text": "When he roasted its heart and licked his burned finger,"
  },
  {
   "from": 3729,
   "to": 3808,
   "text": "he could suddenly understand the birds."
  },
  {
   "from": 3897,
   "to": 3982,
   "text": "For the Church, the dragon was the Devil himself."
  },
  {
   "from": 3984,
   "to": 4093,
   "text": "The Book of Revelation describes a great red dragon with seven heads,"
  },
  {
   "from": 4094,
   "to": 4175,
   "text": "thrown out of heaven by the archangel Michael."
  },
  {
   "from": 4176,
   "to": 4218,
   "text": "Then there's Saint George."
  },
  {
   "from": 4219,
   "to": 4285,
   "text": "The real George was a Roman soldier"
  },
  {
   "from": 4287,
   "to": 4328,
   "text": "who died around the year 303."
  },
  {
   "from": 4330,
   "to": 4379,
   "text": "His dragon didn't join the story"
  },
  {
   "from": 4380,
   "to": 4439,
   "text": "for roughly seven hundred years."
  },
  {
   "from": 4440,
   "to": 4492,
   "text": "The famous version comes from the"
  },
  {
   "from": 4493,
   "to": 4562,
   "text": "Golden Legend, written in the 1260s."
  },
  {
   "from": 4563,
   "to": 4665,
   "text": "Outside a city called Silene, a dragon was fed sheep,"
  },
  {
   "from": 4666,
   "to": 4751,
   "text": "then people, then children chosen by lottery,"
  },
  {
   "from": 4753,
   "to": 4814,
   "text": "until the lot fell on the king's daughter."
  },
  {
   "from": 4815,
   "to": 4905,
   "text": "George wounded the beast with his lance, and the princess"
  },
  {
   "from": 4906,
   "to": 5011,
   "text": "led it into the city on her belt, like a tame dog."
  },
  {
   "from": 5012,
   "to": 5111,
   "text": "Afterwards, it took four ox-carts to drag the body away."
  },
  {
   "from": 5113,
   "to": 5164,
   "text": "The same book tells of a saint who"
  },
  {
   "from": 5166,
   "to": 5224,
   "text": "escaped from inside a dragon's belly."
  },
  {
   "from": 5226,
   "to": 5315,
   "text": "Its own author called that story nonsense."
  },
  {
   "from": 5404,
   "to": 5472,
   "text": "Dragons flew over battlefields too."
  },
  {
   "from": 5474,
   "to": 5544,
   "text": "Roman cavalry rode behind dragon-shaped"
  },
  {
   "from": 5546,
   "to": 5597,
   "text": "banners that hissed in the wind."
  },
  {
   "from": 5599,
   "to": 5660,
   "text": "On the Bayeux Tapestry, a dragon standard"
  },
  {
   "from": 5661,
   "to": 5737,
   "text": "falls beside King Harold at Hastings, in 1066."
  },
  {
   "from": 5738,
   "to": 5807,
   "text": "In a history written in Wales around 830,"
  },
  {
   "from": 5808,
   "to": 5895,
   "text": "a king's tower keeps collapsing, because two dragons"
  },
  {
   "from": 5897,
   "to": 5982,
   "text": "are fighting in a pool beneath it: a red one for"
  },
  {
   "from": 5983,
   "to": 6053,
   "text": "the Britons, and a white one for the Saxons."
  },
  {
   "from": 6054,
   "to": 6115,
   "text": "A boy prophesies that the red will win."
  },
  {
   "from": 6116,
   "to": 6209,
   "text": "Henry Tudor carried that red dragon at Bosworth in 1485,"
  },
  {
   "from": 6210,
   "to": 6309,
   "text": "though it only became the official flag of Wales in 1959."
  },
  {
   "from": 6310,
   "to": 6386,
   "text": "In Poland, the oldest tale of the Wawel Dragon,"
  },
  {
   "from": 6387,
   "to": 6448,
   "text": "from around 1200, has two princes kill it with"
  },
  {
   "from": 6449,
   "to": 6527,
   "text": "a cattle hide stuffed with burning sulphur."
  },
  {
   "from": 6529,
   "to": 6641,
   "text": "Then one prince murders his brother, to take the credit."
  },
  {
   "from": 6733,
   "to": 6791,
   "text": "People also thought they had proof."
  },
  {
   "from": 6793,
   "to": 6868,
   "text": "Around 1335, a huge skull was dug out of a gravel"
  },
  {
   "from": 6870,
   "to": 6926,
   "text": "pit near Klagenfurt, in Austria, and put on"
  },
  {
   "from": 6927,
   "to": 6995,
   "text": "display in the town hall as a dragon's skull."
  },
  {
   "from": 6997,
   "to": 7046,
   "text": "In 1840 it was identified."
  },
  {
   "from": 7047,
   "to": 7112,
   "text": "It belonged to a woolly rhinoceros."
  },
  {
   "from": 7113,
   "to": 7186,
   "text": "The city's stone dragon, carved in the 1590s,"
  },
  {
   "from": 7188,
   "to": 7244,
   "text": "may even have been modelled on it."
  },
  {
   "from": 7245,
   "to": 7299,
   "text": "In the Czech city of Brno,"
  },
  {
   "from": 7301,
   "to": 7376,
   "text": "a dragon still hangs in the old town hall."
  },
  {
   "from": 7377,
   "to": 7441,
   "text": "It's a stuffed Nile crocodile."
  },
  {
   "from": 7442,
   "to": 7486,
   "text": "And in Krak\u00f3w, giant bones hang on"
  },
  {
   "from": 7488,
   "to": 7559,
   "text": "a chain outside the cathedral door."
  },
  {
   "from": 7646,
   "to": 7721,
   "text": "Medieval maps did show dragons,"
  },
  {
   "from": 7723,
   "to": 7801,
   "text": "sometimes coiled beneath the whole world."
  },
  {
   "from": 7802,
   "to": 7861,
   "text": "But the famous phrase \"here be dragons\" appears"
  },
  {
   "from": 7862,
   "to": 7954,
   "text": "on exactly one known object: a copper globe about"
  },
  {
   "from": 7956,
   "to": 8041,
   "text": "the size of a grapefruit, from the early 1500s."
  },
  {
   "from": 8042,
   "to": 8108,
   "text": "Off the coast of Asia, it reads,"
  },
  {
   "from": 8109,
   "to": 8151,
   "text": "in Latin, \"Hic sunt dracones\"."
  },
  {
   "from": 8152,
   "to": 8180,
   "text": "Here are dragons."
  },
  {
   "from": 8181,
   "to": 8281,
   "text": "In 1855, an architect bought it in Paris for almost nothing,"
  },
  {
   "from": 8282,
   "to": 8350,
   "text": "and let his children play with it."
  },
  {
   "from": 8358,
   "to": 8433,
   "text": "So a medieval dragon was many things."
  },
  {
   "from": 8435,
   "to": 8474,
   "text": "A light in the sky."
  },
  {
   "from": 8476,
   "to": 8517,
   "text": "A skull in the gravel."
  },
  {
   "from": 8519,
   "to": 8580,
   "text": "A crocodile from far away."
  },
  {
   "from": 8581,
   "to": 8618,
   "text": "The Devil himself."
  },
  {
   "from": 8620,
   "to": 8690,
   "text": "Most of all, it was the shape people gave"
  },
  {
   "from": 8692,
   "to": 8750,
   "text": "to everything they couldn't explain."
  },
  {
   "from": 8751,
   "to": 8807,
   "text": "If you enjoyed this, subscribe."
  },
  {
   "from": 8809,
   "to": 8874,
   "text": "There are more legends to come."
  }
 ],
